173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 144 0 R
/E (This work presents the analysis of the IEEE 13-Bus unbalanced distribution system by evaluating the p.u. voltage profile and power losses under different operating conditions. The benchmark system is compared with a modified system incorporating additional loads and capacitor compensation under a 24-hour varying load profile. Further, photovoltaic \(PV\) integration is analyzed at weak buses such as Bus 675, 680, 611, and 652 to study voltage regulation and loss reduction. The results show that PV integration improves voltage profile and reduces active and reactive power losses by decreasing feeder current flow. Among the analyzed buses, Bus 675 shows the most effective improvement in voltage stability and loss minimization.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
